WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.600
There's so much to discover on Netflix, ranging&nbsp;
from action to horror to science fiction and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.320
beyond. Sometimes finding the perfect movie for&nbsp;
your mood can be tough. Not to worry, we're here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.640
to help and we've spotlighted some hidden Netflix&nbsp;
gems that you can add to your must-watch list.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.040
Fashion designer Tom Ford scripted&nbsp;
and directed Nocturnal Animals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.240
a mind-bending, and deeply unsettling thriller&nbsp;
in which the plot itself blends, interferes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.600
and gets confused with a story being told by the&nbsp;
film's troubled characters. Amy Adams plays Susan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:34.320
an unhappily married art gallery owner who&nbsp;
receives a fascinating novel manuscript called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.440
Nocturnal Animals, written by her vindictive&nbsp;
first husband, Edward, played by Jake Gyllenhaal.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.720
The action in the film shifts to depict the book,&nbsp;
a horrifying story about Tony, also portrayed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:50.160
Gyllenhaal, a man whose car breaks down in rural&nbsp;
Texas just before a gang of criminals kidnaps his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:55.520
wife and daughter and leaves him stranded. It's&nbsp;
up to Detective Bobby Andes, a strong-but-silent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.240
type to help Tony exact his revenge.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, back in Susan and Edward's world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.320
viewers learn about the emotional devastation&nbsp;
that led to the demise of their marriage.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.120
Neil Pond of Parade called Nocturnal Animals an...

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.120
"Arty and grotesquely gorgeous, but&nbsp;
hardly an uplifting tale. [...] Think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.360
No Country For Old Men meets CSI:&nbsp;
West Texas, by way of Twin Peaks."

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.720
Jason Momoa looks like a superhero in real life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.680
so it's logical he gets to play larger-than-life&nbsp;
figures like Aquaman and physical characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.360
like Khal Drogo on Game of Thrones. These&nbsp;
roles seem like a natural fit for Momoa.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.840
"I dig it."

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.080
In Braven, Momoa gets the opportunity&nbsp;
to play a regular guy for once. Albeit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.720
a regular guy thrust into a stressful&nbsp;
situation and forced to do heroic things.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.480
A humble family man named Joe Braven&nbsp;
takes his father and daughter to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.000
their cabin in the woods to forget&nbsp;
their troubles for a couple of days.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.840
Unfortunately, they don't get any rest&nbsp;
and relaxation because they run afoul&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:53.760
of drug traffickers who have been using&nbsp;
the Braven's property as a stash house.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:59.200
A violent and bloody standoff ensues as Braven&nbsp;
fights to protect his property and his family.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.080
Joe Leydon of Variety&nbsp;
perfectly summed up the film…

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:06.320
"To put it simply and gratefully, Braven&nbsp;
is the sort of unpretentious yet thoroughly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.640
professional popcorn entertainment that&nbsp;
brings out the best in everybody involved."

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.560
A Monster Calls might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.440
sound like the name of a horror movie, but it's&nbsp;
actually a Spielberg-like fantasy. Director J.A.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.400
Bayona crafts an allegorical, eye-popping film&nbsp;
about all-too real and difficult emotions from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:27.360
the point of a view of a child, which makes it all&nbsp;
the more heartbreaking. A Monster Calls is about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:32.000
grief, but it's also about a walking, talking,&nbsp;
tree creature with the voice of Liam Neeson.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.320
Conor is 13, and his mother is dying. He's&nbsp;
just old enough to know what's going on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.800
but young enough to have no idea how to cope;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.520
he can't turn to his stern grandmother for help&nbsp;
and his father isn't a big part of his life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:49.120
An unlikely and impossible ally arrives just when&nbsp;
Conor needs him: He is the Monster, a massive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.720
sentient yew tree who offers to tell Conor three&nbsp;
grand tales. After that, Conor must share his own.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.040
"Stories are wild creatures, Conor O'Malley.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.120
When you let them loose, who&nbsp;
know what havoc they may wreak?"

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:04.560
It's all a little frightening and also&nbsp;
wonderful, and the revelation of where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.960
the tree learned his stories will definitely&nbsp;
leave the viewer misty-eyed, which is rare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:13.840
for a movie about a giant monster who may or&nbsp;
may not be a figment of a child's imagination.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:19.600
Television has been graced with many reality and&nbsp;
game shows that pit a group of strangers against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:25.120
each other, requiring a vote to eliminate all but&nbsp;
one last-standing champion. Alliances are formed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:30.960
but it's ultimately every person for themselves.&nbsp;
The provocative and frightening 2015 film Circle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:36.880
takes the idea and ups the stakes considerably. 50&nbsp;
strangers, all facing execution, are placed in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:42.080
darkened room and made to choose among themselves&nbsp;
which one of them shall get to walk out alive.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:43.040
"It's us."

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:43.680
"Us?"

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.240
"What do you mean?"

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.680
"We're choosing who dies."

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.600
The sparse film's sparse 87&nbsp;
minutes fly by as various unnamed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:55.280
desperate characters passionately&nbsp;
argue and bargain on behalf of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.160
own futures while time and chances run out.&nbsp;
Of course, they also have to fear immediate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:04.560
eradication by the wicked forces holding&nbsp;
them in the room if they so much as move.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.840
John DeFore of The Hollywood Reporter&nbsp;
wrote about the film, saying...

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:12.000
"[Circle] keeps suspense alive, building&nbsp;
to a final tableau that, silently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.920
says nearly as much about human nature&nbsp;
as does all the talk leading up to it."

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:21.440
At the beginning of Elizabeth Harvest, the film&nbsp;
seems like an examination of a newlywed couple's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.640
life. Henry and Elizabeth Kellenberg appear to be&nbsp;
delicately adjusting to life as married people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:31.040
Elizabeth moves into the wealthy and prominent&nbsp;
Henry's beautiful, well-appointed home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:35.280
filled with luxuries and creature comforts.&nbsp;
In the spirit of their new partnership,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:39.360
Henry gives Elizabeth free rein over his&nbsp;
house, and suggests that they'll live in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:44.000
wedded bliss so long as she doesn't go poking&nbsp;
around one mysterious room in the basement.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.120
"That sounds ominous."

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:50.800
Naturally, Elizabeth can't help herself and&nbsp;
investigates the forbidden zone. This is when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:56.000
film takes a turn and gets really interesting. She&nbsp;
discovers a shocking secret that sends her down a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:01.200
mysterious path filled with danger and intrigue.&nbsp;
With elements of science fiction and horror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.680
Elizabeth Harvest is a dark fairytale&nbsp;
that explores man's darkest impulses.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.360
War movies are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:12.240
by their nature, action movies. The best ones&nbsp;
re-create true events with emotional honesty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:17.520
and visceral realism that exposes viewers to an&nbsp;
approximation of the nightmarish world of combat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:23.120
The Outpost is such a movie, taking place during&nbsp;
the Battle of Kamdesh, a crucial, and deadly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:29.440
2009 event in the ongoing Afghanistan War. At the&nbsp;
Keating combat outpost, set in a valley of three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:35.040
mountains, outnumbered American soldiers fight&nbsp;
an onslaught of well-armed Taliban combatants.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.120
Presented as a series of episodes, The&nbsp;
Outpost doesn't just re-create an epic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:43.120
battle from recent history, but it tells&nbsp;
a story which allows the audience to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:47.440
to know the characters. The members of the&nbsp;
troop are mostly just regular, decent people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:52.160
thrust into a difficult and clearly terrifying&nbsp;
situation, with everything leading up to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:57.120
can't-look-away battle scenes. In fact, Matt&nbsp;
Fowler of IGN described The Outpost as...

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:59.840
"A cleverly, and respectfully, crafted war film."

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:05.280
Knock Knock is a home invasion thriller with a&nbsp;
couple of twists. The criminals have an important,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:09.200
if cynical, lesson to teach about the&nbsp;
baseness of men, and it's also one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:14.080
the few movies where the universally beloved&nbsp;
Keanu Reeves plays an unlikeable character.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:19.120
This dread-inducing and quick-moving 2015&nbsp;
thriller from writer-director Eli Roth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:23.680
begins innocuously with a knock on the door&nbsp;
of the beautiful home of seemingly happily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:28.480
married architect Evan Webber. Because of work&nbsp;
obligations, he's home alone, with his dog,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:32.080
Monkey, over Father's Day while&nbsp;
his family takes a quick vacation.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:37.760
Genesis and Bel, two young, flirtatious women,&nbsp;
played by Lorenza Izzo and a pre-Knives Out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:42.160
Ana de Armas, gain entry, claiming to&nbsp;
be lost and looking for a house party.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:46.080
"Not everyone would just let two total&nbsp;
strangers into their house these days."

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.600
"Well, you don't look that dangerous."

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:53.200
The women aggressively come on to&nbsp;
Evan, and he eventually gives in to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:57.040
his base carnal urges — and that's&nbsp;
when the terror and violence begin.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:01.600
Knock Knock is actually a light&nbsp;
remake of the 1977 B-movie Death Game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:05.920
which has gained a cult following in the years&nbsp;
since its release. Just like the original,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:10.640
this film is packed with thrills, suspense,&nbsp;
humor and over-the-top performances.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:13.440
An elite squad of secret operatives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:18.160
hunting down and punishing those who committed&nbsp;
unspeakable acts of terror against their community&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:22.880
is a small film genre unto itself — and&nbsp;
a good one at that. Among such stories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:28.160
one can find as much action and drama as cathartic&nbsp;
psychology and shocking real-world history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:33.200
In the same vein of Steven Spielberg's Munich,&nbsp;
which told the story of Israeli Mossad agents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:39.600
going after the terrorists who killed athletes at&nbsp;
the 1972 Summer Olympics, comes Operation Finale.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:43.920
The film details the early '60s mission&nbsp;
of a team of highly-trained, top secret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:49.200
Israeli operatives who travel to Argentina&nbsp;
in order to bring to justice Adolf Eichmann.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.840
He was a high-ranking Nazi official who&nbsp;
masterminded the logistics of the Holocaust,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:57.840
responsible for the deaths of millions&nbsp;
of Jewish people. Oscar Isaac plays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:02.560
real-life Mossad agent Peter Malkin,&nbsp;
leading the charge against Eichmann.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.840
M.V. Moorhead of Phoenix&nbsp;
Magazine called Operation Finale…

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:10.000
"Crisp and absorbing and satisfying,&nbsp;
both as a thriller and as a moral drama."

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:12.720
On one level, viewers know exactly what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.480
they're getting when they click on a&nbsp;
movie called Vampires vs. the Bronx.

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:18.480
"We got vampires in the Bronx."

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:22.560
It is indeed a violent tale of creepy&nbsp;
bloodsuckers hailing from Eastern Europe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:27.280
in the classic vampire movie style. But this&nbsp;
time, they're in a modern-day urban setting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:32.880
specifically one of New York City's five boroughs.&nbsp;
However, Vampires vs. the Bronx is so much more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:38.160
than that — it's a socially conscious celebration&nbsp;
of Bronx culture, the story of a bunch of smart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:43.120
and capable kids coming together to save the&nbsp;
day, and a deeply satirical horror-comedy.

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:47.920
The vampiric real estate agents at the center&nbsp;
of the story represent wealthy individuals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.960
and businesses that want to&nbsp;
gentrify older neighborhoods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:55.760
and a scrappy bunch of young people have to stop&nbsp;
them before nothing is left and no one is alive.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:56.880
"Don't go there, Ma."

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:59.280
"He's...he's a really bad man."

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:01.280
"Of course he is, he's in real estate."

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:04.400
Like many critics, Ben Travis&nbsp;
of Empire had positive things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.600
to say about Vampires vs. the&nbsp;
Bronx. He called the film...

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.320
"A witty and likable horror-comedy that manages to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.920
put a stake to the heart of some real&nbsp;
issues while it tickles your ribs."

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:17.040
Based on Joe Ballarini's series of gently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:19.200
spooky kids novels of the same name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:24.880
The Babysitter's Guide to Monster Hunting is a&nbsp;
family-friendly movie directed by Rachel Talalay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:29.840
a filmmaker best known for her work on Tank&nbsp;
Girl and the Nightmare on Elm Street series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:34.800
Ballarini and Talalay were the ideal combo to&nbsp;
make what could be a kid's first horror-comedy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:39.840
a dark, funny, and twisted take on the&nbsp;
'80s classic Adventures in Babysitting.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:45.040
Teenage babysitter Kelly gets a gig looking after&nbsp;
a kid on Halloween night. That's a bummer in and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:50.400
of itself, made worse when the child is kidnapped&nbsp;
by the actual Boogeyman. Kelly has to do her best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:54.720
to rescue the little guy. Luckily, she's helped&nbsp;
along the way in her fight against monsters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:59.680
goblins, and pure evil by a secret society&nbsp;
of elite and well-equipped babysitters.

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.320
"Ugh, I hate babysitters."

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:04.880
Nell Minnow of Movie Mom said the film delivers...

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:07.600
"Gorgeously imagined settings, a great cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:12.640
and an exciting story that hits the exact sweet&nbsp;
spot between funny-scary and scary-funny."

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:16.960
The 12th Man is a war movie, a&nbsp;
survival tale, and, amazingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:22.240
it's also a true story. Jan Baalsrud worked for&nbsp;
the Norwegian resistance during Nazi Germany's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:27.360
occupation of his country during World War II.&nbsp;
Trained as a commando by the British military,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:32.960
Baalsrud attempts an escape to neutral Sweden&nbsp;
following a sabotage mission gone wrong. To get to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:38.160
freedom, he has to face the punishing weather of&nbsp;
Scandinavia in the winter. The Norway-based Nazis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:43.120
however, notice almost immediately that Baalsrud&nbsp;
has disappeared and chase him through the icy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:48.800
mountains, where conditions are so severe that&nbsp;
frostbite and hypothermia may claim him first.

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:53.040
Among many other positive reviews, Frank&nbsp;
Sheck of The Hollywood Reporter wrote...

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.480
"The 12th Man proves consistently&nbsp;
engrossing and suspenseful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:59.840
with its lead performances&nbsp;
further enhancing its impact."

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:03.680
The best horror movies consist of a&nbsp;
lot more than just a few jump scares&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:07.920
and some terrifying form of bone-chilling&nbsp;
menace — the good ones reflect and comment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:12.560
upon the everyday things that trouble human&nbsp;
beings. Little Evil is that kind of movie.

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:15.200
It's a horror-comedy, with the emphasis on comedy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:19.520
about an eager-to-please guy who marries a&nbsp;
woman who has a son from a previous marriage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:24.080
He's desperate to connect with the inscrutable&nbsp;
little guy so his relationship can thrive and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:29.200
can all come together as a happy family. That's a&nbsp;
difficult task, as the kid is actually the spawn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:34.640
of Satan and he's not afraid to unleash pure evil&nbsp;
and terror on his well-meaning new stepdad. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:39.280
that's where the horror comes into play; that,&nbsp;
and with a creepy hand-puppet named Reeroy.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.840
"I'm your step-father now."

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.000
"Get out."

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:46.960
"Yeah, okay. We'll just talk&nbsp;
later or whenever you want."

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:52.240
Amanda Sink of The Hollywood Outsider&nbsp;
perfectly described the film in one line.

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:55.360
"Little Evil is [The] Omen&nbsp;
by way of Shaun of the Dead."

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.840
Check out one of our newest&nbsp;
videos right here! Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:01.440
even more Looper videos about&nbsp;
movies on Netflix are coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:09.840
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit&nbsp;
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

